========== 5. JF-5 — what R5.6 actually says, and what it does not ==========
[R19 PASS] R5.6's title is *Secret redaction in output*
[R20 PASS] R5.6 governs MASKING SECRET VALUES IN OUTPUT
[R21 PASS] R5.6 says nothing about argv, a process listing or /proc — revision 1 cited it as the rule REQUIRING the stdin handoff, which it is not. It is motivation (the standard's posture on exposing secret values), and the operative reasons are that argv is world-readable on Linux via /proc/<pid>/cmdline and that ARG_MAX bounds a payload.


